# armour/<body>/skirt_split: SPLIT, a coat skirt in two long smooth panels parted at the front: this part is
# the waist over the hips; the panels' tails to the ankle are skirt_split_back (layer back, behind the legs).
# Generated from the FORGE-LIMBS skirt templates (gen_skirts2.py, skirts_def.py; iteration 2: the D view serves U, `tags anyfacing`); Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
# (INTEGRATE silhouettes i2) STARFALL (forge-starfall) gilds the lower edge of the tails facing D and the waist lame's lower row
# facing R and L (its glint cell kept): the T6 hero's trim where the shield hides the front (C12 b).
# (FORGE-LIMBS envelope r1) T5-T6 skirt flare (STYLE_P2 29.3): `armour.t5` views facing D/U, 1 px more past the hips on the lower half; flared copies of the replace views go before them. Generated by FORGE-LIMBS flare.py.
use person
body woman
role overlay skirt.split
layer hangFront
anchor hip
keys hang
tags anyfacing
z 10

view D key rest origin 9 0
|.vyyyzyyvvxwwwwwv.
|.vxxxxxxvvxwwwwwv.
|vxxxxxv....vwwwwwv
|vyyyyv......vxxxxv
regions
